//@version=6
// BOS Buy/Sell Signals
// Break-of-structure entry signals built from "long/short candles" plus a confirmed BOS break.
//
// Pattern (long; short is mirrored):
//   1. A LONG candle forms - a green candle closing above the previous red candle's high.
//   2. Look back `lookback` bars for a LOCAL LOW that sits below the candle body.
//   3. The BOS is the highest high strictly between that local low and the long candle.
//      If there are no bars between them there is no structure, so the setup is ignored.
//   4. An ALERT triangle is drawn on the long candle: something may happen here.
//   5. A SECOND long candle must form, and the PEAK STRICTLY BETWEEN the two candles
//      must exceed the BOS by delta 3 (`bosDelta`) - the sensitivity that rejects weak
//      impulses. Optionally (`reqPullback`) that peak must also sit above candle 2's own
//      high by `pullPct` percent, so there is a real pullback rather than a straight
//      run into candle 2.
//      Candle 2 must also have OPENED and CLOSED clear of the BOS - optionally by a
//      percentage margin (`c2Clear`) - so a candle that merely wicks past the level
//      cannot confirm.
//      The second candle must be at least `minGap` bars after the first, so the
//      break of the BOS has time to be confirmed. Opposite candles appearing in
//      between are ignored - they do not reset the setup. Price trading back beyond
//      the local extreme DOES reset it: for a long, any low below the local low from
//      step 2 means the structure that framed the setup is gone (dipping below candle 1
//      alone does not). So does price coming back down to the BOS, on any bar before
//      candle 2, after it had HELD above it - the peak cleared it by delta 3 and
//      `holdBars` bars in a row closed above it: the entry level has already been
//      retested without a signal. A spike above the BOS that falls straight back is a
//      failed break, not a hold, and coming back from it does not reset the setup. Candle 2 itself may wick into the BOS - only its
//      body has to stay clear.
//      Optionally (`c2Break`) candle 2 may make the break itself instead: its high clears
//      the BOS by delta 3 and it closes above it (it may open below), with no break before it.
//      Such a break must then HOLD: the BUY is drawn only after `holdBars` further bars that
//      all stay above the BOS. Price touching the BOS before that resets the setup.
//   6. BUY is drawn at the BOS level on the second candle; STOP below the lowest low from
//      candle 1 up to candle 2 - candle 1's own low, or a lower dip between the candles.
//      If price never trades into the entry..stop band within `fillWindow` bars of candle 1, those
//      drawings are erased again, so unreachable signals do not clutter the history.
//   7. The trade is entered only once price comes back into the entry..stop band after
//      the signal; a signal not reached within `fillWindow` bars of candle 1 lapses without an
//      exit. There is no fixed take profit. An entered position is closed by whichever
//      comes first:
//      - the opposite signal;
//      - an opposite candle (a short candle for a long) closing at or beyond the 25%
//        Fibonacci retracement of the impulse after the fill: from the lowest low since
//        the fill to the highest high printed after that low. The impulse only counts
//        once it is at least as tall as the entry-to-stop distance, so chop right after
//        the fill cannot trigger it. It is tracked internally and is not drawn or
//        configurable.
//      A position stopped out below the STOP line simply ends, without an exit marker.
//
// Every qualifying candle arms its own setup. Several can be open at the same time, in
// the same direction or in opposite ones, and each confirms or expires independently -
// an open setup never suppresses a later one.

indicator("BOS Buy/Sell Signals", overlay = true, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_bars_back = 500)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- inputs
//
// Three deltas drive the pattern. The first two are horizontal (time), so they are set
// in bars. The third is vertical (price), so bars cannot express it - it takes a unit.
//
grp1 = "Delta 1 - lookback for local high/low + BOS (bars)"
lookback   = input.int(20, "Lookback before candle 1", minval = 2, maxval = 200, group = grp1,
     tooltip = "How many bars left of the trigger candle to search for the local extreme. The BOS is then the furthest price between that extreme and candle 1.")
minStruct  = input.int(2, "Min bars between extreme and candle 1", minval = 2, maxval = 50, group = grp1,
     tooltip = "A BOS needs room to form. With 2, a local low sitting on the bar immediately before candle 1 is ignored, because nothing structural sits between them.")

grp2 = "Delta 2 - distance between candle 1 and candle 2 (bars)"
minGap     = input.int(3, "Min bars between candle 1 and candle 2", minval = 2, maxval = 100, group = grp2,
     tooltip = "The confirming candle must be at least this many bars after the trigger candle, so the BOS break has time to be confirmed. Minimum 2, because at least one bar must sit between the two candles for the intervening peak to exist. A same-direction candle arriving earlier neither confirms nor resets the setup - it is skipped.")
maxWait    = input.int(50, "Max bars to wait for confirmation", minval = 1, maxval = 500, group = grp2,
     tooltip = "Upper bound on the same distance. The setup expires if candle 2 has not arrived within this many bars.")
reqPullback = input.bool(false, "Require pullback off the peak/trough", group = grp2,
     tooltip = "On: the peak between the two candles must sit above candle 2's high (below its low for shorts), so there is a genuine pullback rather than a straight run into candle 2. Off: candle 2 may itself make the extreme. Only affects confirmation - the peak is still measured strictly between the candles for delta 3 either way.")
pullPct    = input.float(0.0, "Peak/trough clearance beyond candle 2 (%)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.01, group = grp2,
     tooltip = "How far the extreme between the two candles must stand beyond candle 2 - the peak above candle 2's HIGH for longs, the trough below its LOW for shorts - as a percentage of candle 2's own extreme. 0 means any margin counts, which makes the pullback barely noticeable; raise it to demand a real one. Only applies while the checkbox above is on.")

grp3 = "Delta 3 - distance between BOS and the peak (price)"
bosUnit    = input.string("Percent", "Measure break distance in", options = ["Percent", "ATR multiple", "Ticks", "Price"], group = grp3,
     tooltip = "This delta is vertical, not horizontal, so it cannot be set in bars. Percent travels well across symbols; ATR multiple also adapts to current volatility.")
bosDelta   = input.float(0.15, "BOS break distance", minval = 0.0, step = 0.01, group = grp3,
     tooltip = "How far beyond the BOS the peak between candle 1 and candle 2 must reach for the break to count as confirmed. Read in the unit selected above.")
c2Clear    = input.float(0.0, "Candle 2 body clearance beyond BOS (%)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.01, group = grp3,
     tooltip = "Candle 2 must OPEN and CLOSE beyond the BOS - above it for longs, below it for shorts. 0 means the body only has to be on the correct side, which is the usual setting. Raise it to demand a margin, as a percentage of the BOS price. Always a percentage, regardless of the unit chosen above.")
c2Break    = input.bool(false, "Allow candle 2 to break the BOS itself", group = grp3,
     tooltip = "Off: the BOS must be broken by delta 3 BETWEEN candle 1 and candle 2, and candle 2 confirms after the pullback. On: additionally, candle 2 may make the break itself - its high (low for shorts) clears the BOS by delta 3 and it closes beyond the BOS - it may open on the near side, even if price stayed on the near side of the BOS in between. The pullback requirement does not apply to such a candle 2. Its break must then HOLD: the signal appears only after the number of bars set in 'Closes beyond BOS to count as a hold' have all stayed beyond the BOS. If price comes back to the BOS before that, the setup is reset.")
holdBars   = input.int(3,"Closes beyond BOS to count as a hold", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = grp3,
     tooltip = "A return to the BOS before candle 2 kills the setup only if price had first HELD beyond it: the break reached delta 3 AND this many consecutive bars closed beyond the BOS. A spike through the BOS that falls straight back is a failed break, not a hold, so coming back from it does not count as a retest and the setup stays alive.")
atrLen     = input.int(14, "ATR length", minval = 1, maxval = 200, group = grp3,
     tooltip = "Only used when a delta is measured in ATR multiples.")

grpS = "Stop"
stopUnit   = input.string("Percent", "Measure stop buffer in", options = ["Percent", "ATR multiple", "Ticks", "Price"], group = grpS)
stopBuffer = input.float(0.05, "Stop buffer", minval = 0.0, step = 0.01, group = grpS,
     tooltip = "Extra room beyond the stop anchor - the lowest low (highest high for shorts) from candle 1 up to candle 2. Read in the unit selected above.")

grpD = "Debug"
debugMode  = input.bool(false, "Explain rejected setups", group = grpD,
     tooltip = "Marks every bar where a setup was rejected, reset or suppressed, with the reason - below the bar for longs, above it for shorts. Resets (expired, broke local low/high, BOS retested, break did not hold) are drawn in gray along the bottom of the pane for longs and the top for shorts. Works across the whole history. When several setups are open, the reason shown is the one from the newest setup. Use it to find out why an expected signal is missing, then turn it off.")

grpL = "Limits"
maxOpen    = input.int(20, "Max simultaneous setups per direction", minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = grpL,
     tooltip = "Safety cap so a long quiet stretch cannot accumulate unbounded setups. The oldest is dropped when the cap is reached.")
onePerDir  = input.bool(true, "One signal per direction", group = grpL,
     tooltip = "On: after a BUY, further BUYs are suppressed until the long is closed (by a SELL or the fib exit), and vice versa - only the first signal of each leg is drawn. The setup itself is still consumed. Off: every confirmation draws its own signal.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- unit conversion
atrVal = ta.atr(atrLen)

// Converts a delta expressed in the chosen unit into a price distance at `level`.
f_off(float level, string unit, float amount) =>
    switch unit
        "Percent"      => level * amount / 100
        "ATR multiple" => atrVal * amount
        "Ticks"        => syminfo.mintick * amount
        => amount

grpV = "Display"
lineLen     = input.int(8, "Signal line length (bars)", minval = 1, maxval = 50, group = grpV)
showAlerts  = input.bool(true, "Show alert triangles", group = grpV)
showCandles = input.bool(true, "Show long/short candle markers", group = grpV,
     tooltip = "Small circles on every detected long/short candle, whether or not it starts a setup. Use these to check the candle definition against the chart.")
showBos     = input.bool(true, "Show BOS levels", group = grpV)
showExits   = input.bool(true, "Show exit markers", group = grpV)
fillWindow  = input.int(100, "Remove unfilled signals after (bars)", minval = 25, maxval = 500, group = grpV,
     tooltip = "Counted from candle 1. If price never trades into the band between the entry and the stop within this many bars of candle 1, that signal's entry, stop and BOS drawings are erased. Keeps old unreachable signals from cluttering the history. A signal that IS reached is kept permanently. An unreached signal also stops counting as an open position, so it produces no exit marker.")

fadeUnfilled = input.bool(true, "Fade signals while price has not reached them", group = grpV,
     tooltip = "A signal still waiting for price to come back into the entry..stop band grows fainter the longer it waits - bright right after candle 1, barely visible near the end of the window above - and is then erased. Once price reaches it, it stays for good at the shade it had at that moment - so on the history a bright signal was reached quickly and a faint one only late.")

cBuy  = input.color(color.new(#26a69a, 0), "Buy", group = grpV, inline = "c")
cSell = input.color(color.new(#ef5350, 0), "Sell", group = grpV, inline = "c")
cStop = input.color(color.new(#ff9800, 0), "Stop", group = grpV, inline = "c")
cBos  = input.color(color.new(#787b86, 40), "BOS", group = grpV, inline = "c")
cExit = input.color(color.new(#ffd600, 0), "Exit", group = grpV, inline = "c")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- candle classification
//
// Long candle  (bullish): a GREEN candle closing above the previous RED candle's HIGH.
// Short candle (bearish): a RED candle closing below the previous GREEN candle's LOW.
//
// This is the definition used in retest_of_retest_indicator.pine, which states it one
// bar back as close[1] > high[2]; evaluated on the candle itself it is the same pattern,
// just recognised as soon as the candle closes rather than one bar later.
//
isLongCandle  = close[1] < open[1] and close > open and close > high[1]
isShortCandle = close[1] > open[1] and close < open and close < low[1]

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- drawn signals awaiting a fill
// A signal whose entry/stop band price never reaches is erased `fillWindow` bars after candle 1.
type Pending
    int   bar       // candle 1 - the fill window counts from here
    int   dir       // 1 long, -1 short
    float entry
    float stop
    line  lnEntry
    line  lnStop
    line  lnBos
    label lbEntry
    label lbStop

var array<Pending> pend = array.new<Pending>()

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- state
// One entry per open setup, held in parallel arrays.
var array<int>   lBarA  = array.new_int()     // bar_index of candle 1
var array<float> lBosA  = array.new_float()   // BOS level
var array<float> lRefA  = array.new_float()   // lowest low from candle 1 up to now - stop anchor
var array<float> lExtA  = array.new_float()   // the local low before candle 1 - the setup dies below it
var array<float> lPeakA = array.new_float()   // highest high STRICTLY BETWEEN candle 1 and now
var array<int>   lHoldA = array.new_int()     // consecutive closes above the BOS; frozen once it reaches holdBars
var array<int>   lC2A   = array.new_int()     // bar of a candle 2 that broke the BOS itself, waiting for the hold; na otherwise
var array<line>  lLineA = array.new<line>()   // the dotted BOS line, so it can be removed with the setup

var array<int>   sBarA    = array.new_int()
var array<float> sBosA    = array.new_float()
var array<float> sRefA    = array.new_float() // highest high from candle 1 up to now - stop anchor
var array<float> sExtA    = array.new_float() // the local high before candle 1
var array<float> sTroughA = array.new_float() // lowest low STRICTLY BETWEEN candle 1 and now
var array<int>   sHoldA   = array.new_int()   // consecutive closes below the BOS
var array<int>   sC2A     = array.new_int()
var array<line>  sLineA   = array.new<line>()

var int   posDir    = 0      // 1 long, -1 short, 0 flat - set by the signal, live or not yet
var bool  posFilled = false  // price has traded into the entry..stop band - the trade is actually on
var int   posBar    = na     // bar of candle 1 - the fill window counts from here
var float posEntry  = na     // BOS level - the entry
var float posStop   = na
var float posBase   = na     // fib 0: worst price since the fill
var float posExt    = na     // fib 100: best price AFTER posBase printed; na until price turns
var float posExtC   = na     // best CLOSE after posBase - measures the impulse, so a lone wick cannot

buySignal  = false
sellSignal = false
longAlert  = false
shortAlert = false
exitLong   = false   // an open long was closed by an opposite signal or the fib exit
exitShort  = false
lDbg       = 0       // debug: why a long candle was rejected on this bar - first reason wins
sDbg       = 0
lKill      = 0       // debug: why a long setup was reset on this bar - kept apart so it is never masked
sKill      = 0

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- fib exit
// A signal is only a trade once price trades back into the entry..stop band, on a bar
// after the signal. A signal not reached within `fillWindow` bars of candle 1 lapses
// silently - nothing was entered, so there is nothing to exit.
//
// From the fill on, the impulse is measured in time order. For a long its 0 is the lowest
// low since the fill, and its 100 is the highest high printed AFTER that low. While price
// keeps making new lows there is no impulse yet - each new low restarts it, and a bar
// making a new low contributes nothing to the high, since within one bar the high may
// have come first. Once the impulse exists, an opposite candle closing at or beyond its
// 25% retracement closes the position. A bar that extends the high is folded in first,
// so a candle that makes a new high and then reverses 25% also counts. Trading through
// the stop ends the position without an exit marker.
//
// Chop right after the fill prints small local highs and lows, and a fib drawn over them
// is noise. So the impulse only counts once it is at least as tall as the trade's risk
// (entry to stop) - until then an opposite candle does not close the position. Its height
// is measured to the best CLOSE, not the best high, so a single wick cannot switch it on;
// the fib levels themselves still use the high/low.
fibExitLevel  = 0.25
fibMinImpulse = 1.0    // minimum impulse height, in multiples of the entry-to-stop distance

if posDir != 0 and not posFilled
    bool hit = posDir == 1 ? (low <= posEntry and high >= posStop)
                           : (high >= posEntry and low <= posStop)
    if hit
        posFilled := true
        posBase   := posDir == 1 ? low : high
        posExt    := na
        posExtC   := na
        if posDir == 1 ? low <= posStop : high >= posStop
            posDir := 0                          // filled and stopped on the same bar
    else if bar_index - posBar > fillWindow
        posDir := 0
else if posDir == 1
    if low <= posStop
        posDir := 0                              // stopped out
    else if low < posBase
        // still falling: a new low restarts the impulse, its high can only come later
        posBase := low
        posExt  := na
        posExtC := na
    else
        if na(posExt) or high > posExt
            posExt := high
        posExtC := na(posExtC) ? close : math.max(posExtC, close)
        if isShortCandle and posExtC - posBase >= fibMinImpulse * (posEntry - posStop)
             and close <= posExt - (posExt - posBase) * fibExitLevel
            exitLong := true
            posDir   := 0
else if posDir == -1
    if high >= posStop
        posDir := 0
    else if high > posBase
        posBase := high
        posExt  := na
        posExtC := na
    else
        if na(posExt) or low < posExt
            posExt := low
        posExtC := na(posExtC) ? close : math.min(posExtC, close)
        if isLongCandle and posBase - posExtC >= fibMinImpulse * (posStop - posEntry)
             and close >= posExt + (posBase - posExt) * fibExitLevel
            exitShort := true
            posDir    := 0

f_dropLong(int k) =>
    line ln = array.get(lLineA, k)
    if not na(ln)
        line.delete(ln)
    array.remove(lBarA, k)
    array.remove(lBosA, k)
    array.remove(lRefA, k)
    array.remove(lExtA, k)
    array.remove(lPeakA, k)
    array.remove(lHoldA, k)
    array.remove(lC2A, k)
    array.remove(lLineA, k)

f_dropShort(int k) =>
    line ln = array.get(sLineA, k)
    if not na(ln)
        line.delete(ln)
    array.remove(sBarA, k)
    array.remove(sBosA, k)
    array.remove(sRefA, k)
    array.remove(sExtA, k)
    array.remove(sTroughA, k)
    array.remove(sHoldA, k)
    array.remove(sC2A, k)
    array.remove(sLineA, k)

// Fades `c` by `f` (0 = as chosen, 1 = invisible), keeping its own transparency as the floor.
f_fade(color c, float f) =>
    color.new(c, color.t(c) + (100 - color.t(c)) * math.min(f, 1.0) * 0.9)

// Repaints a waiting signal's drawings `f` of the way towards invisible.
f_paint(Pending p, float f) =>
    color cDir = p.dir == 1 ? cBuy : cSell
    line.set_color(p.lnEntry, f_fade(cDir, f))
    line.set_color(p.lnStop, f_fade(cStop, f))
    if not na(p.lnBos)
        line.set_color(p.lnBos, f_fade(cBos, f))
    label.set_color(p.lbEntry, f_fade(cDir, f))
    label.set_textcolor(p.lbEntry, f_fade(color.white, f))
    label.set_color(p.lbStop, f_fade(cStop, f))
    label.set_textcolor(p.lbStop, f_fade(color.white, f))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- retire signals price never reached
// While a signal waits for price, its drawings fade with age - bright right after candle 1,
// barely visible near the end of `fillWindow` - and are erased once the window runs out.
// When price does reach it the shade freezes, so on the history a bright signal was
// reached quickly and a faint one only late.
if array.size(pend) > 0
    for k = array.size(pend) - 1 to 0
        Pending p = array.get(pend, k)
        // did this bar trade anywhere inside the entry..stop band?
        bool filled = p.dir == 1 ? (low <= p.entry and high >= p.stop)
                                 : (high >= p.entry and low <= p.stop)
        if filled
            // reached - kept for good, frozen at the shade it had when price got there
            if fadeUnfilled
                f_paint(p, float(bar_index - p.bar) / fillWindow)
            array.remove(pend, k)
        else if bar_index - p.bar > fillWindow
            line.delete(p.lnEntry)
            line.delete(p.lnStop)
            if not na(p.lnBos)
                line.delete(p.lnBos)
            label.delete(p.lbEntry)
            label.delete(p.lbStop)
            array.remove(pend, k)
        else if fadeUnfilled
            f_paint(p, float(bar_index - p.bar) / fillWindow)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- long: evaluate open setups
// Walked back to front so entries can be removed without disturbing pending indices.
if array.size(lBarA) > 0
    for k = array.size(lBarA) - 1 to 0
        int   b  = array.get(lBarA, k)
        float bs = array.get(lBosA, k)
        float rf = array.get(lRefA, k)    // lowest low of candle 1 .. bar_index-1
        float lx = array.get(lExtA, k)    // local low
        float st = rf - f_off(rf, stopUnit, stopBuffer)
        float pk = array.get(lPeakA, k)   // covers bars b+1 .. bar_index-1; na while empty
        int   hd = array.get(lHoldA, k)   // closes above the BOS, bars b+1 .. bar_index-1
        int   c2 = array.get(lC2A, k)     // self-breaking candle 2 waiting for its hold, or na
        bool  held = hd >= holdBars

        // The peak is tested BEFORE this bar is folded into it, so a candle 2 that makes
        // the high itself cannot satisfy the rule - there must be a genuine pullback.
        bool gapOk   = isLongCandle and bar_index - b >= minGap
        bool haveP   = not na(pk)
        bool pullOk  = not reqPullback or (haveP and pk >= high * (1 + pullPct / 100))
        bool breakOk = haveP and pk >= bs + f_off(bs, bosUnit, bosDelta)
        // optional: candle 2 makes the break itself, with no break-and-pullback before it
        bool selfBrk = c2Break and high >= bs + f_off(bs, bosUnit, bosDelta)
        // candle 2 must have opened AND closed clear of the BOS, not just wicked past it
        bool bodyOk  = math.min(open, close) >= bs * (1 + c2Clear / 100)
        // a candle 2 breaking the BOS itself opens below it, so only its close has to clear
        bool closeOk = close >= bs * (1 + c2Clear / 100)

        // price must not trade below the local low the structure was built from; if it
        // does the structure that framed the setup is gone, so the setup is reset. Dipping
        // below candle 1 alone is fine.
        bool drop = false
        bool fire = false
        if bar_index - b > maxWait or low < lx
            lKill := lKill == 0 ? (bar_index - b > maxWait ? 1 : 2) : lKill
            drop := true                                 // expired or invalidated
        else if not na(c2)
            // candle 2 broke the BOS itself, so the signal waits until price has HELD above
            // it for holdBars bars. Coming back to the BOS before that means the break did
            // not hold, and the setup is reset.
            if low <= bs
                lKill := lKill == 0 ? 5 : lKill
                drop := true
            else if bar_index - c2 >= holdBars
                fire := true
        else if gapOk and haveP and pullOk and breakOk and bodyOk
            fire := true
        else if gapOk and selfBrk and closeOk
            array.set(lC2A, k, bar_index)                // start waiting for the hold
        else if breakOk and held and low <= bs
            // price broke above the BOS (delta 3), HELD there (holdBars closes in a row) and
            // came back down to it before candle 2: the retest of the entry level happened
            // without a signal, so the setup is spent. A spike above that falls straight
            // back is a failed break, not a hold, so coming back from it does not count.
            lKill := lKill == 0 ? 4 : lKill
            drop := true
        else
            if gapOk
                lDbg := lDbg == 0 ? (not breakOk and not selfBrk ? (haveP ? 7 : 5) : breakOk and not pullOk and not selfBrk ? 6 : 8) : lDbg
            else if isLongCandle
                lDbg := lDbg == 0 ? 9 : lDbg

        if fire
            if not onePerDir or posDir != 1
                buySignal := true
                if posDir == -1 and posFilled
                    exitShort := true
                posDir    := 1
                posFilled := false
                posBar    := b
                posEntry  := bs
                posStop   := st
                line  lnE = line.new(bar_index, bs, bar_index + lineLen, bs, color = cBuy, width = 2)
                line  lnS = line.new(bar_index, st, bar_index + lineLen, st, color = cStop, width = 2)
                label lbE = label.new(bar_index + lineLen, bs, "BUY", style = label.style_label_left, color = cBuy, textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
                label lbS = label.new(bar_index + lineLen, st, "STOP", style = label.style_label_left, color = cStop, textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
                array.push(pend, Pending.new(b, 1, bs, st, lnE, lnS, array.get(lLineA, k), lbE, lbS))
                array.set(lLineA, k, na)     // the BOS line now belongs to the Pending record
            else
                lDbg := lDbg == 0 ? 3 : lDbg
            drop := true

        if drop
            f_dropLong(k)
        else
            array.set(lPeakA, k, na(pk) ? high : math.max(pk, high))
            array.set(lRefA, k, math.min(rf, low))   // a dip below candle 1 moves the stop under it
            array.set(lHoldA, k, held ? hd : close > bs ? hd + 1 : 0)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- long: arm a new setup
// Runs after the evaluation above, so this bar's candle can confirm an earlier setup
// and start a new one at the same time.
if isLongCandle
    float locLow    = na
    int   locLowOff = na
    for i = 1 to lookback
        if na(locLow) or low[i] < locLow
            locLow    := low[i]
            locLowOff := i
    // the local low must sit below the trigger candle body, and leave room for structure
    bool okLow  = not na(locLow) and locLow < math.min(open, close)
    bool okRoom = not na(locLowOff) and locLowOff >= minStruct
    float bos = na
    if okLow and okRoom
        for i = 1 to locLowOff - 1
            if na(bos) or high[i] > bos
                bos := high[i]
    // a BOS only counts if price has not already cleared it
    bool okBos = not na(bos) and bos > close
    if not (okLow and okRoom and okBos)
        lDbg := lDbg == 0 ? (not okLow ? 10 : not okRoom ? 11 : na(bos) ? 12 : 13) : lDbg
    if okLow and okRoom and okBos
        if array.size(lBarA) >= maxOpen
            f_dropLong(0)                            // drop the oldest
        array.push(lBarA, bar_index)
        array.push(lBosA, bos)
        array.push(lRefA, low)
        array.push(lExtA, locLow)
        array.push(lPeakA, na)      // no bars between candle 1 and now yet
        array.push(lHoldA, 0)
        array.push(lC2A, na)
        line bosLn = na
        if showBos
            bosLn := line.new(bar_index - locLowOff, bos, bar_index, bos, color = cBos, style = line.style_dotted)
        array.push(lLineA, bosLn)
        longAlert := true

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- short: evaluate open setups
if array.size(sBarA) > 0
    for k = array.size(sBarA) - 1 to 0
        int   b  = array.get(sBarA, k)
        float bs = array.get(sBosA, k)
        float rf = array.get(sRefA, k)      // highest high of candle 1 .. bar_index-1
        float hx = array.get(sExtA, k)      // local high
        float st = rf + f_off(rf, stopUnit, stopBuffer)
        float tr = array.get(sTroughA, k)   // covers bars b+1 .. bar_index-1; na while empty
        int   hd = array.get(sHoldA, k)
        int   c2 = array.get(sC2A, k)
        bool  held = hd >= holdBars

        bool gapOk   = isShortCandle and bar_index - b >= minGap
        bool haveT   = not na(tr)
        bool pullOk  = not reqPullback or (haveT and tr <= low * (1 - pullPct / 100))
        bool breakOk = haveT and tr <= bs - f_off(bs, bosUnit, bosDelta)
        bool selfBrk = c2Break and low <= bs - f_off(bs, bosUnit, bosDelta)
        bool bodyOk  = math.max(open, close) <= bs * (1 - c2Clear / 100)
        bool closeOk = close <= bs * (1 - c2Clear / 100)

        bool drop = false
        bool fire = false
        if bar_index - b > maxWait or high > hx
            sKill := sKill == 0 ? (bar_index - b > maxWait ? 1 : 2) : sKill
            drop := true
        else if not na(c2)
            // candle 2 broke the BOS itself: wait for the hold, reset if price comes back
            if high >= bs
                sKill := sKill == 0 ? 5 : sKill
                drop := true
            else if bar_index - c2 >= holdBars
                fire := true
        else if gapOk and haveT and pullOk and breakOk and bodyOk
            fire := true
        else if gapOk and selfBrk and closeOk
            array.set(sC2A, k, bar_index)
        else if breakOk and held and high >= bs
            // price broke below the BOS, held there and came back up to it
            sKill := sKill == 0 ? 4 : sKill
            drop := true
        else
            if gapOk
                sDbg := sDbg == 0 ? (not breakOk and not selfBrk ? (haveT ? 7 : 5) : breakOk and not pullOk and not selfBrk ? 6 : 8) : sDbg
            else if isShortCandle
                sDbg := sDbg == 0 ? 9 : sDbg

        if fire
            if not onePerDir or posDir != -1
                sellSignal := true
                if posDir == 1 and posFilled
                    exitLong := true
                posDir    := -1
                posFilled := false
                posBar    := b
                posEntry  := bs
                posStop   := st
                line  lnE = line.new(bar_index, bs, bar_index + lineLen, bs, color = cSell, width = 2)
                line  lnS = line.new(bar_index, st, bar_index + lineLen, st, color = cStop, width = 2)
                label lbE = label.new(bar_index + lineLen, bs, "SELL", style = label.style_label_left, color = cSell, textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
                label lbS = label.new(bar_index + lineLen, st, "STOP", style = label.style_label_left, color = cStop, textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
                array.push(pend, Pending.new(b, -1, bs, st, lnE, lnS, array.get(sLineA, k), lbE, lbS))
                array.set(sLineA, k, na)     // the BOS line now belongs to the Pending record
            else
                sDbg := sDbg == 0 ? 3 : sDbg
            drop := true

        if drop
            f_dropShort(k)
        else
            array.set(sTroughA, k, na(tr) ? low : math.min(tr, low))
            array.set(sRefA, k, math.max(rf, high))
            array.set(sHoldA, k, held ? hd : close < bs ? hd + 1 : 0)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- short: arm a new setup
if isShortCandle
    float locHigh    = na
    int   locHighOff = na
    for i = 1 to lookback
        if na(locHigh) or high[i] > locHigh
            locHigh    := high[i]
            locHighOff := i
    bool okHigh = not na(locHigh) and locHigh > math.max(open, close)
    bool okRoom = not na(locHighOff) and locHighOff >= minStruct
    float bos = na
    if okHigh and okRoom
        for i = 1 to locHighOff - 1
            if na(bos) or low[i] < bos
                bos := low[i]
    bool okBos = not na(bos) and bos < close
    if not (okHigh and okRoom and okBos)
        sDbg := sDbg == 0 ? (not okHigh ? 10 : not okRoom ? 11 : na(bos) ? 12 : 13) : sDbg
    if okHigh and okRoom and okBos
        if array.size(sBarA) >= maxOpen
            f_dropShort(0)
        array.push(sBarA, bar_index)
        array.push(sBosA, bos)
        array.push(sRefA, high)
        array.push(sExtA, locHigh)
        array.push(sTroughA, na)    // no bars between candle 1 and now yet
        array.push(sHoldA, 0)
        array.push(sC2A, na)
        line bosLn = na
        if showBos
            bosLn := line.new(bar_index - locHighOff, bos, bar_index, bos, color = cBos, style = line.style_dotted)
        array.push(sLineA, bosLn)
        shortAlert := true

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- plots
plotshape(showCandles and isLongCandle, title = "Long candle", style = shape.circle,
     location = location.belowbar, color = color.new(color.green, 70), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(showCandles and isShortCandle, title = "Short candle", style = shape.circle,
     location = location.abovebar, color = color.new(color.red, 70), size = size.tiny)

plotshape(showAlerts and longAlert, title = "Long alert", style = shape.triangleup,
     location = location.belowbar, color = color.new(#ffeb3b, 0), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(showAlerts and shortAlert, title = "Short alert", style = shape.triangledown,
     location = location.abovebar, color = color.new(#ffeb3b, 0), size = size.tiny)

plotshape(showExits and exitShort, title = "Exit short", style = shape.xcross,
     location = location.belowbar, color = cExit, size = size.large)
plotshape(showExits and exitLong, title = "Exit long", style = shape.xcross,
     location = location.abovebar, color = cExit, size = size.large)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- debug
// Plot shapes rather than labels: labels are capped at the 500 most recent, which hides
// the reasons on older history. Orange = candle 2 rejected, maroon = candle 1 rejected,
// blue = signal suppressed by "One signal per direction" - all at the bar. Gray = setup
// reset, drawn along the bottom (longs) / top (shorts) of the pane so the candle labels
// cannot hide it.
plotshape(debugMode and lKill == 1, "Dbg L 1", shape.labelup, location.bottom, color.new(color.gray, 30), text = "expired", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and lKill == 2, "Dbg L 2", shape.labelup, location.bottom, color.new(color.gray, 30), text = "broke local low", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and lDbg == 3, "Dbg L 3", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.new(color.blue, 30), text = "already long", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and lKill == 4, "Dbg L 4", shape.labelup, location.bottom, color.new(color.gray, 30), text = "BOS retested", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and lKill == 5, "Dbg L K5", shape.labelup, location.bottom, color.new(color.gray, 30), text = "break did not hold", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and lDbg == 5, "Dbg L 5", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.new(color.orange, 30), text = "no peak between", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and lDbg == 6, "Dbg L 6", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.new(color.orange, 30), text = "no pullback", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and lDbg == 7, "Dbg L 7", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.new(color.orange, 30), text = "break < delta 3", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and lDbg == 8, "Dbg L 8", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.new(color.orange, 30), text = "close/body not above BOS", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and lDbg == 9, "Dbg L 9", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.new(color.orange, 30), text = "too early", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and lDbg == 10, "Dbg L 10", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.new(color.maroon, 30), text = "no local low", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and lDbg == 11, "Dbg L 11", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.new(color.maroon, 30), text = "local low too close", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and lDbg == 12, "Dbg L 12", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.new(color.maroon, 30), text = "no BOS", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and lDbg == 13, "Dbg L 13", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.new(color.maroon, 30), text = "BOS already cleared", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and sKill == 1, "Dbg S 1", shape.labeldown, location.top, color.new(color.gray, 30), text = "expired", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and sKill == 2, "Dbg S 2", shape.labeldown, location.top, color.new(color.gray, 30), text = "broke local high", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and sDbg == 3, "Dbg S 3", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.new(color.blue, 30), text = "already short", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and sKill == 4, "Dbg S 4", shape.labeldown, location.top, color.new(color.gray, 30), text = "BOS retested", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and sKill == 5, "Dbg S K5", shape.labeldown, location.top, color.new(color.gray, 30), text = "break did not hold", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and sDbg == 5, "Dbg S 5", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.new(color.orange, 30), text = "no trough between", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and sDbg == 6, "Dbg S 6", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.new(color.orange, 30), text = "no pullback", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and sDbg == 7, "Dbg S 7", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.new(color.orange, 30), text = "break < delta 3", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and sDbg == 8, "Dbg S 8", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.new(color.orange, 30), text = "close/body not below BOS", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and sDbg == 9, "Dbg S 9", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.new(color.orange, 30), text = "too early", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and sDbg == 10, "Dbg S 10", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.new(color.maroon, 30), text = "no local high", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and sDbg == 11, "Dbg S 11", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.new(color.maroon, 30), text = "local high too close", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and sDbg == 12, "Dbg S 12", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.new(color.maroon, 30), text = "no BOS", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)
plotshape(debugMode and sDbg == 13, "Dbg S 13", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.new(color.maroon, 30), text = "BOS already cleared", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, display = display.pane)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- alerts
alertcondition(buySignal,  "BOS Buy",  "BOS buy signal")
alertcondition(sellSignal, "BOS Sell", "BOS sell signal")
alertcondition(longAlert,  "BOS Long setup",  "Long setup armed - watching for BOS break")
alertcondition(shortAlert, "BOS Short setup", "Short setup armed - watching for BOS break")
